Fly's start as the 3DS plays it (Port_FlyIntro, 3ds_port/src/3ds_game_full.c)
in place of the field move's banner and the bird out of the ball: from the
ball pose the Pokemon doing the Fly comes out on the ground beside the player,
small and white and growing into its colours with its cry and a few sparkles;
the player turns and hops onto its back; it lifts off, hanging on while the
cinematic's camera climbs (Port_FlyHover), then goes on as the bird's own
fly-off. follower_mon.c tells where the Fly sprite's feet are
(FollowerMon_FlyFeet), to stand it on the ground. Without a sprite for the
Pokemon the GBA's start plays from its banner on.
Applies after 0086-fly-sky-supply.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

